===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A type of thin south Indian [[pancake]] made from [[ferment]]ed [[lentil]]s and [[rice]] blended with water, typically served with [[chutney]] or [[sambar]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Aravind Adiga|title=The White Tiger|publisher=Atlantic|year_published=2009|page=141
|passage=I carried the Mongoose's bags to the right carriage of the train, then went to a stall and bought a '''''dosa''''', wrapped in paper, for him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Meg Cotner|title=Food Lovers' Guide to Queens|publisher=Rowman & Littlefield|isbn=9780762792597|page=173|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=2vs0tibCmWkC&pg=PA173&dq=%22dosa%22+wrap&hl=&cd=4&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22dosa%22%20wrap&f=false|text=These condiments are provided as something for you to dip your '''''dosa''''' into. The '''''dosa''''' wrap itself has a slight tang to it, as it is a fermented bread made from rice and lentils, and is light and delicious.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Mary Jo Murphy|title=Dosas, Big and Bigger|work=The New York Times|date=2013-06-14|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2013/06/16/nyregion/a-review-of-chennai-dosas-restaurant-in-hicksville.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=The '''dosas''' all came with coconut chutney and sambar, a lentil broth — good dipping condiments.}}

